<title>ITALY: Italian bank bad loans up slightly in Feb - BoI.</title>
<headline>Italian bank bad loans up slightly in Feb - BoI.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bad loans in the Italian banking system rose 0.68 percent to 115.444 trillion lire in February from 114.657 trillion in January, latest Bank of Italy figures showed.</p>
<p>On a year-on-year basis, bad loans rose 3.53 percent from 111.503 trillion lire in February 1996.</p>
<p>The ratio of bad loans to total bank loans in February equalled 10.5 percent against 10.4 percent in January.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
